Package: basinmodlR
Type: Package
Title: One-Dimensional Burial and Thermal History Modelling of Sedimentary Basins
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Michiel",
                  family = "Arts",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu")
Description: Forward modelling of the burial, compaction and temperature history
    of a sedimentary column through geological time. A basin is described by one
    row per stratigraphic unit and one row per erosion event; deposition phases,
    hiatuses, layer stacks, maximum-burial windows and grain (solid) thicknesses
    are all derived from that description. Compaction follows an exponential
    porosity-depth law and is treated as irreversible, so uplifted layers keep the
    porosity acquired at their deepest burial. Temperatures follow the
    steady-state conductive geotherm for a layered column with radiogenic heat
    production. Utilities are provided to check the continuity of the results, to
    determine when a unit is inside a hydrocarbon generation window, and to draw a
    composite burial and temperature figure. Input tables for three localities in
    the Anglo-Brabant Massif and the Ardennes are included.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: graphics, grDevices, stats, utils
